shown on the edition's line breaks, would settle where the line begins."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5054,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5054},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21d7509a-0984-40d8-9208-d8197481a644","uuid":"f29532e5-19a6-4efa-a32e-2c3607d12e8e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:43:12.724Z","request_id":"req_011CgjZcPYXCeJrgVZsc1xzq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Gh3AD1xPvquYCT1tEJZ3P2":{"working":"The line opens with a double barline, the alto clef and one flat. The first stretch runs from about x=160 to the stroke at about x=325, which I read as a barline. It is short and has no slur: roughly two hooked 8th figures and an 'r'-shaped quarter rest. That fits the tail of bar 27 (A3 8th, A3 8th, rest 8th, rest quarter). The slurred G3–A3 pair that opens bar 27 is not visible, so the line probably begins partway into bar 27. That bar still counts as the line's. The next stretch runs to the stroke at about x=775, which I take as bar 28. It shows an 8th rest, a beamed group of three 8ths around middle C under one slur (C#4 D4 E4), a single 8th (D4), an 8th rest, and an 'r'-shaped quarter rest. That is bar 28's six events. The last stretch runs to the final double barline, which I take as bar 29. It shows an 8th rest, two beamed 8ths low in the staff (C#4 C#4), and a slurred group of four 32nds, triple-beamed, higher in the staff (A4 G4 F4 E4). Then come a quarter (D4) and a quarter rest under a fermata, which ends the bar as the edition does. Things that don't match: a stray note-like mark sits below the staff under bar 29, likely a correction or cue. The 'f' at the top right belongs to the li